<h2>Asobi 1.0 (build 1843) <span class="when">Oct 26, 2026</span></h2>
<ul>
<li><b>Showcases on other Macs are marked</b>: in the Review Manager, a showcase under On Other Macs has the yellow Showcase tag and its finished / viewers count, as your own do. Click it for its viewing.</li>
</ul>
<hr>
<div class="earlier">Earlier updates</div>
<h3>1.0 (build 1840) <span class="when">Oct 26, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Other Macs&#8217; reviews on their own page</b>: in the Review Manager, clicking a review under On Other Macs shows it on the right, with the studio&#8217;s controls (Join, Pause, Only People Invited, End) and its viewing straight away, as your own reviews do.</li>
</ul>
<h3>1.0 (build 1837) <span class="when">Oct 26, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Autonomy&#8217;s own showcase visits aren&#8217;t counted</b>: visits from a connection a studio Mac uses, or from a browser marked as ours, are listed dimmed with an Autonomy tag and left out of every figure, the studio-wide figures and Google Analytics. No notifications for them either.</li>
<li><b>Mark a phone or laptop as ours</b>: the new button in Showcase figures copies a link; open it once on a device and its showcase visits are never counted. The link works for 30 days.</li>
<li><b>Clear your marks from the web</b>: guests have a Clear button in the drawing tools and can right-click the picture for Clear My Marks on This Frame.</li>
</ul>
<h3>1.0 (build 1833) <span class="when">Oct 26, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Every studio Mac&#8217;s showcases in Studio Reviews</b>: studio Macs now register their reviews and showcases with the studio by default (an admin who turned it off stays off), and live showcases are registered once even when their host has closed, so they appear under On Other Macs.</li>
<li><b>Showcase figures, tidied</b>: one set of columns down the whole panel (visits, time watched, watched to the end, clicked the closing link; hover a symbol for its name), full names on hover, one row per showcase, and the panel stays open if you leave it open.</li>
</ul>
<h3>1.0 (build 1830) <span class="when">Oct 26, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Fixed: showcases collect viewing again.</b> A showcase made on a Mac that holds the studio license wasn&#8217;t registered with the review server, so nobody&#8217;s viewing was recorded and its figures stayed empty. Showcases now register correctly, and Asobi registers your live showcases again each time it opens, so ones already sent start recording from then on. Viewing from before this update wasn&#8217;t kept.</li>
<li><b>Showcases report to the studio&#8217;s analytics</b>, whichever studio Mac made them.</li>
</ul>
<h3>1.0 (build 1827) <span class="when">Oct 24, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Marked frames go to Kitsu as attachments</b>: the pictures sent with live notes and with Publish Review are now attached to their comment, so they no longer take the shot&#8217;s next revision number away from the next version.</li>
</ul>
<h3>1.0 (build 1824) <span class="when">Oct 24, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Reviews in Open Recent</b>: every review you share is listed under its name, and choosing it reopens the review, as Reopen in the Review Manager does. Switching optimized media on or off no longer adds the clip on screen to the list.</li>
<li><b>Save and Save As, plainly</b>: both write the session (.otio). Save writes to the file the session came from; Save As asks for a name and place. The playlist&#8217;s Export Timeline is now Save As too.</li>
</ul>
<h3>1.0 (build 1820) <span class="when">Oct 24, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Save works with several windows open</b>: each window keeps its own saved state, so Save in one is no longer undone by another, and quitting asks only about the windows that really have unsaved changes, by name.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
